      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added a mix of very small nits, that are only worth doing if we keep this change, and larger structural changes and questions.  I am also in the process of finishing https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/963157, which will significantly simplify RenderPassDesc and other texture format handling so may be of interest to you if it changes how these blit pipelines are keyed.\n\nOn the other hand, I\u0027m also wanting to know more about the expected timeline for the dawn extension to support resolving to a smaller texture. How much time is there likely to be to go from this to the extension, and then remove all of this code? Or does this also likely benefit all platforms when operating in the context of WASM where we don\u0027t have transient attachments, so they will want to benefit from approx-size attachments via this emulation?",
