      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T19:44:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure we want to commit to actually doing multiple render passes here. I believe we can take this code path if we are running WASM+WebGPU and don\u0027t have access to the various dawn extensions. This could easily be on platforms that would regress performance-wise or run into correctness issue (but perhaps not, since transient attachments are one of those extensions, so loading and storing is possible still).\n\nIf I\u0027m understanding this correctly, we are no longer copying the resolve texture into a separate single-channel texture. Before we would do: 1) blit (resolve-\u003ecopy), render (draw w/ copy, ..., resolve) and now we do: 1) render (draw resolve to color) 2) render (..., store color) 3) render (draw color to resolve).\n\nIf we aren\u0027t resolving in the main render pass, I don\u0027t think we need to have a separate intermediate render pass at the start. There shouldn\u0027t be any more restriction of just sampling the resolve texture at the start of the main render pass.  It would mean that the blit-as-draw pipeline needs to handle depth/stencil attachments as part of its key though.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 463,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 469,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "b2740cd1cc06998eaa340fc6fcb04af43e10475c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6636ac42_e39a3194",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnLoadResolveWithDrawHelper.cpp",
