        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T19:44:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The actual srcSampleCount doesn\u0027t need to be part of the key, right? It\u0027s really whether or not we use the shader that performs the for loop or not, the actual sample count is provided by the `textureNumSamples` intrinsic.  We could push that farther and say always use the `kLoadMultisampledFSText` and assume it degrades to the single-sampled load automatically.  Would have to measure performance to see how much that loop generation costs us though.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "b2740cd1cc06998eaa340fc6fcb04af43e10475c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
